  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lockheed Martin obligated $10.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 146 awards, with an average award size of $72.9M. Obligations rose up 2.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a multi-year trend: FY21 was $4.7B, FY22 was $7.1B, FY23 was $8.7B, FY24 was $7.3B, FY25 was $10.4B, and FY26 was $10.6B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market, accounting for $9.6B of FY2026 to date obligations. Other notable NAICS markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $91.7M. Lockheed Martin’s FY2026 to date totals are partial, meaning current-year totals reflect fiscal year to date contract obligations rather than full-year totals. This snapshot highlights concentration in a single market and continued year-over-year growth in obligations compared with the prior fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is Lockheed Martin's FY2026 federal business?",
        "body": "Lockheed Martin obligated $10.6B in FY2026 to date across 146 awards, with an average award size of $72.9M. Obligations were up 2.1% year over year, and FY2026 to date is a partial total for the fiscal year. Fiscal-year history shows growth from $4.7B in FY21 to $10.6B in FY26, with FY25 at $10.4B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Lockheed Martin's obligations concentrate?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $9.6B of FY2026 to date obligations. Other concentration points include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $91.7M, with a long tail of smaller NAICS markets."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Lockheed Martin make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Lockheed Martin obligated $10.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for $9.6B of those obligations, and the company recorded 146 awards with an average award size of $72.9M. Fiscal-year obligations rose up 2.1% year over year, and prior fiscal years were $4.7B in FY21, $7.1B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, $7.3B in FY24, and $10.4B in FY25."
